              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "browser",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CDN",
                    "sub": "edge",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "App",
                    "sub": "local or Redis",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Database",
                    "sub": "buffer pool",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cache ==as close to the user== as correctness allows",
                "Each layer outward is faster but {red:staler}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Pick for",
                "Catch"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Cache-aside**",
                  "read-heavy default",
                  "first read misses"
                ],
                [
                  "**Write-through**",
                  "consistency",
                  "slower writes"
                ],
                [
                  "**Write-back**",
                  "write throughput",
                  "loss if cache dies"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Eviction and Invalidation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Eviction",
                  "==LRU== default; LFU for stable hot sets"
                ],
                [
                  "Bound staleness",
                  "==TTL== always"
                ],
                [
                  "Dynamic data",
                  "TTL plus delete on write"
                ],
                [
                  "Static assets",
                  "version keys, `app.3f9a.js`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Stampede Defense",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Single-flight lock==: one request rebuilds, others wait",
                "==TTL jitter==: base plus random, no shared expiry",
                "==Serve stale== while revalidating",
                "==Null caching== for missing keys, short TTL"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Delete, do not set",
              "text": "After the DB update, ==delete== the key. A set can race and store a stale value."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Writers A and B update key k. Order: A writes DB, B writes DB, B sets cache, A sets cache. What do DB and cache hold?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "DB holds B's value, cache holds A's, so it is stale until the TTL.",
                "Fix: delete the key after the DB write; the next read refills it."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "5,000 hot keys are cached at startup with ttl=300. What happens at 300 s?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "All expire together, so the misses hit the DB at once: a stampede.",
                "Fix: TTL jitter (base + random) and a single-flight lock per key."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Redis is full with volatile-lru, but no key has a TTL. What does a write do?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It fails with an error.",
                "volatile-* evicts only keys with a TTL, so there is no victim, same as noeviction."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Cache-aside looks up user -1, which is not in the DB. Why does every request hit the DB?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Nothing is found, so nothing is cached and each request misses.",
                "Fix: cache a null with a short TTL, or use a Bloom filter."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
